==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*ǵr̥h₂nóm}}.  Cognates include Old Irish {{term|grán|lang=sga}}, Breton {{term|greun|lang=br}}, Old Church Slavonic {{term|зрьно|tr=zrĭno|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}}, Lithuanian {{term|žirnis|žìrnis|pea|lang=lv}}, Persian {{term|sc=fa-Arab|خرمن|tr=xarman||grain|lang=fa}} and Old English {{term|corn||grain|lang=ang}} (English {{term|corn|lang=en}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-pronunc|grānum}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|grānum||grānī|n|second}}

# a [[grain]], [[seed]] or [[small]] [[kernel]]

